# Trivy ignore list — HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs we accept on the published images.
#
# Format: one CVE/GHSA per line, optional comment after. Trivy reads this
# at the repo root automatically (also passed explicitly to the scan
# action in .github/workflows/docker-scan.yml).
#
# Policy:
#  - We never ignore CVEs in code Diluxite executes against untrusted
#    input (HTTP bodies, MCP tool args, markdown content, etc.).
#  - We prefer fixing at the source over ignoring. Add an entry here only
#    when a HIGH/CRITICAL lives in tooling that never runs on user data and
#    cannot be patched/removed, and pair it with a tracking note.
#
# Currently empty: the recurring pnpm-bundle findings (corepack's vendored
# copies of tar / minimatch / picomatch / brace-expansion / ip-address, and
# pnpm itself) are gone because the runtime images no longer ship any package
# manager — the API launches with `node --import tsx` and the Dockerfiles
# rm -rf the npm + corepack trees. pnpm now only runs in the discarded builder
# stage, which Trivy never scans. (This closes the former alpha.8 TODO.)
